{#-
  gemma4.jinja — byte-exact Gemma-4 turn renderer for ghostwriter-rs.

  ============================ TOKEN-BYTE PROVENANCE ============================
  The literal token bytes below are transcribed from _research/07 §2.4 and
  _research/05 §2 (per the pinned `google/gemma-4-12B-it` chat_template.jinja):

    turn  OPEN  : "<|turn>" ~ role ~ "\n"     (ASYMMETRIC pipe — NOT <start_of_turn>)
    turn  CLOSE : "<turn|>\n"                  (ASYMMETRIC pipe — NOT <end_of_turn>)
    thought OPEN: "<|channel>thought\n"        (ASYMMETRIC — NOT symmetric <|channel|>)
    thought CLOSE: "<channel|>"                (ASYMMETRIC)
    BOS         : emitted by the template as the literal "<bos>" first byte.

  A `model` turn ALWAYS carries a thought wrapper: it holds the reasoning when
  supervised/masked, or is EMPTY ("<|channel>thought\n<channel|>") when stripped.
  The model turn render is therefore byte-exact:
    "<|turn>model\n<|channel>thought\n{reasoning}\n<channel|>{answer}<turn|>\n"
  (supervised) or
    "<|turn>model\n<|channel>thought\n<channel|>{answer}<turn|>\n"  (stripped).

  Roles map to `user` and `model` only (assistant -> model). There is NO system
  role: system content is folded into the FIRST user turn by the Rust caller
  before this template runs (see render::gemma4). This is the harness simplification
  of the upstream conditional-system-turn behavior and is documented there.

  TODO(gemma4-verify): these bytes are per the _research spec. Before production
  SFT they MUST be diff-verified byte-for-byte against the official pinned
  `google/gemma-4-12B-it` chat_template.jinja (do NOT fetch at runtime / in tests).
  ==============================================================================

  Context shape (provided by render::gemma4):
    turns : [ { role: "user" | "model",
                content: str,
                reasoning: str | None } ]   # None => empty thought wrapper (stripped)
-#}
{{- "<bos>" -}}
{%- for turn in turns -%}
{{- "<|turn>" ~ turn.role ~ "\n" -}}
{%- if turn.role == "model" -%}
{{- "<|channel>thought\n" -}}
{%- if turn.reasoning is not none -%}
{{- turn.reasoning ~ "\n" -}}
{%- endif -%}
{{- "<channel|>" -}}
{%- endif -%}
{{- turn.content -}}
{{- "<turn|>\n" -}}
{%- endfor -%}
